  "id": "antipredator-defense",
  "term": "antipredator defense",
  "definition": "Antipredator defense is behavior that helps an animal reduce the chance of being successfully attacked by a predator. In the source material, it refers to displays such as tail movements that draw a predator’s attention away from more vulnerable body parts and may also support warning or chemical defenses.",
